    <div class="split__text prose">
      <h2 class="section-title">Why one person, start to finish?</h2>
      <p>I'm a one-man business, and that's deliberate. The person who comes to measure your room is the person who draws it, chooses the timber, cuts the joints and fits the last piece. Nothing gets lost between a salesperson, a designer and a fitting team, because there aren't any.</p>
      <p>It also means I take on a limited number of projects at a time, and each one gets my full attention. I'd rather do fewer jobs properly than rush any of them.</p>
      <p>The furniture I make uses the best materials and fittings I can get, and it's built to last. Traditional or contemporary, whether it's a whole kitchen or a single bookcase, I'd be glad to talk it through.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

